      hallazgo: 'According to Búsqueda, Spain\'s Asesores Financieros Andalucía Occidental (AFAO), a minority shareholder through Bimper, registered an arbitration against Uruguay on 29 July 2025 before the World Bank\'s International Centre for Settlement of Investment Disputes (ICSID), invoking the 1992 Uruguay-Spain bilateral investment treaty. The original claim, filed in 2009, was for 272.7 million euros; the case is backed by the firm Dechamps International Law, with offices in the United Kingdom, Argentina and Uruguay. El Observador reported on 19 February 2026 that German arbitrator Stephan Schill, an expert in international arbitration and international public law, accepted his appointment by the claimant, and that the firm is claiming US$ 383 million from the Uruguayan State. On 12 May 2026 the same outlet reported that the tribunal was completed with Canada\'s Meg Kinnear, appointed by Uruguay, and Chile\'s Felipe Bulnes Serrano as president.',
