      contexto: 'On 6 May 2026, ahead of the Legislative Palace\'s centenary, Vice President Carolina Cosse presented, alongside architect Salvador Schelotto and other technical staff, an urban intervention project: an annex building of some 2,600 square metres with a library, reading rooms, a CAIF childcare centre, student housing and an accessible public plaza on its roof, plus improvements to public space and the urban integration of the surroundings. According to Montevideo Portal, Parliament had earmarked US$ 40 million for centenary works and returned US$ 30 million to general revenue, leaving about US$ 10 million available.',
